From: EglantinePS5 <noreply@eglantineps5.local>
Subject: [PATCH] Migrate 0400-black-world-01-upscale-stand-in-same-size-copy.patch

Source: 0400-black-world-01-upscale-stand-in-same-size-copy.patch
(EDEN_NX2_UPSCALE_SAME_SIZE)

Ocarina of Time with its Max Resolution patch in Handheld renders 3D at the output's 1920x1080.
Its network's last pass (first HMMA at 0xc00, rejected) then reads and writes 1920x1080 images.
The stand-in only accepted pairs the output enlarges (to_width > from_width), found none,
logged "no input/output image pair in the program's handles or cbuf0+0x80..0x11c", and the
dispatch was dropped: the output image stayed black while the HUD, drawn later, showed
(run74). The same program in Docked still upscales 1920x1080 to 2560x1440 and found its pair
(run75, "plain copy" at 106 s).

EDEN_NX2_UPSCALE_SAME_SIZE=1: among the program's own read and store handles a pair of one
size counts too. The drawn frame (E5B9G9R9) is taken first: another read of the output's size
and format may be the network's own last output (a temporal network's history), and copying
that would leave the output as it started. A same-size pair keeps its input (the 0048 swap for
"an image only rejected passes fill" does not apply to a drawn frame), and is logged once:
"Upscale fallback for program ...: same-size copy ... -> ...". The title-4, Fortune's Weave,
Bananza and blind cbuf0 scans keep asking for an upscale: there any two same-size images of
one format would pair. Unset, nothing changes.

Lichii (nx2 5a50f50) never reaches this: it lowers HMMA in software for every program
(lower_to_maxwell.h 0x23c "software warp expansion", emit_spirv_tensor.cpp), which is our
EDEN_NX2_TENSOR=compact form, so on Linux the network itself ran.

Checked: clang syntax check against the T20 tree (e736dfd + 0001-0399). Not built, not run.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
 src/video_core/engines/kepler_compute.cpp | 51 ++++++++++++++++++++---
 1 file changed, 45 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/video_core/engines/kepler_compute.cpp b/src/video_core/engines/kepler_compute.cpp
index 9eb5943beb..161cc7247a 100644
--- a/src/video_core/engines/kepler_compute.cpp
+++ b/src/video_core/engines/kepler_compute.cpp
@@ -949,8 +949,17 @@ bool KeplerCompute::UpscaleInsteadOfNativeProgram() {
     };
     // An upscale keeps the aspect ratio and scales by at most 4: anything else (a 4x4 lookup
     // table, a 120x67 luminance image) is another image the program happens to use.
+    // EDEN_NX2_UPSCALE_SAME_SIZE=1: the program's own read and store handles may also pair images
+    // of one size. Ocarina of Time with its Max Resolution patch in Handheld renders 3D at the
+    // output's 1920x1080, and its network (first HMMA at 0xc00) then reads and writes 1920x1080
+    // images: with upscales only, no pair was found, the dispatch was dropped and the output image
+    // stayed black (run74). The same program in Docked still upscales 1920x1080 to 2560x1440 and
+    // found its pair (run75). Only the program's own handles may pair same-size images: in the
+    // cbuf0 scans below any two same-size images of one format would do.
+    static const bool same_size_ok = std::getenv("EDEN_NX2_UPSCALE_SAME_SIZE") != nullptr;
     const auto upscale_pair = [](const std::optional<Texture::TICEntry>& from,
-                                 const std::optional<Texture::TICEntry>& to, bool same_format = true) {
+                                 const std::optional<Texture::TICEntry>& to, bool same_format = true,
+                                 bool same_size = false) {
         if (!from || !to || (same_format && from->format != to->format) || from->Address() == 0 ||
             to->Address() == 0 || from->Address() == to->Address() || !from->IsBlockLinear() ||
             !to->IsBlockLinear())
@@ -958,7 +967,9 @@ bool KeplerCompute::UpscaleInsteadOfNativeProgram() {
         const u64 from_width = from->Width(), from_height = from->Height();
         const u64 to_width = to->Width(), to_height = to->Height();
         const u64 cross_a = to_width * from_height, cross_b = to_height * from_width;
-        return from_width >= 64 && to_width > from_width && to_width <= from_width * 4 &&
+        const bool scales = to_width > from_width ||
+                            (same_size && to_width == from_width && to_height == from_height);
+        return from_width >= 64 && scales && to_width <= from_width * 4 &&
                (cross_a > cross_b ? cross_a - cross_b : cross_b - cross_a) * 32 <= cross_a;
     };
     std::optional<Texture::TICEntry> input = image(0x90), output = image(0xa0);
@@ -977,10 +988,24 @@ bool KeplerCompute::UpscaleInsteadOfNativeProgram() {
         output.reset();
         for (const u32 store : stores) {
             const auto to = image(store);
+            // Same-size pairs: the drawn frame (E5B9G9R9, Ocarina of Time) first. Of the program's
+            // other reads of the output's size, one of its format may be its own last output (a
+            // temporal network's history): copying that would leave the output as it started.
+            if (same_size_ok) {
+                for (const u32 read : reads) {
+                    const auto from = image(read);
+                    if (from && from->format == Texture::TextureFormat::E5B9G9R9 &&
+                        upscale_pair(from, to, false, true)) {
+                        input = from;
+                        output = to;
+                        break;
+                    }
+                }
+            }
             for (const bool same_format : {true, false}) {
                 for (const u32 read : reads) {
                     const auto from = image(read);
-                    if (upscale_pair(from, to, same_format) &&
+                    if (upscale_pair(from, to, same_format, same_size_ok) &&
                         (!input || u64{from->Width()} * from->Height() > u64{input->Width()} * input->Height())) {
                         input = from;
                         output = to;
@@ -990,15 +1015,29 @@ bool KeplerCompute::UpscaleInsteadOfNativeProgram() {
             }
             if (input) break;
         }
+        const bool same_size_pair = input && output && input->Width() == output->Width() &&
+                                    input->Height() == output->Height();
+        if (same_size_pair) {
+            static std::unordered_set<GPUVAddr> reported;
+            if (reported.insert(regs.code_loc.Address()).second) {
+                LOG_INFO(HW_GPU, "Upscale fallback for program {:#x}: same-size copy {:#x} format {} {}x{} -> {:#x} format {}",
+                         regs.code_loc.Address(), input->Address(),
+                         static_cast<u32>(input->format.Value()), input->Width(), input->Height(),
+                         output->Address(), static_cast<u32>(output->format.Value()));
+            }
+        }
         // The last pass of a rejected network can read an image only the rejected passes fill
         // (Ocarina of Time's title and movies): the frame is then another image of that size in
         // cbuf0 that upscales to the same output, which is what the scan below used to find.
         // EDEN_NX2_UPSCALE_KEEP_FRAME=1 leaves an E5B9G9R9 input alone. That is Ocarina of Time's
         // gameplay frame: draws fill it (run68), so the reason above doesn't apply to it, and
         // without this it gives way to a B10G11R11 image its handle scan doesn't list.
+        // A same-size pair keeps its input too: the frame it reads is drawn, not filled by
+        // rejected passes, and another image of that size is as likely the network's own output.
         static const bool keep_drawn_frame = std::getenv("EDEN_NX2_UPSCALE_KEEP_FRAME") != nullptr;
         const bool keep_input =
-            keep_drawn_frame && input && input->format == Texture::TextureFormat::E5B9G9R9;
+            same_size_pair ||
+            (keep_drawn_frame && input && input->format == Texture::TextureFormat::E5B9G9R9);
         for (u32 slot = 0x80; input && !keep_input && slot < 0x120; slot += 4) {
             const auto from = memory_manager.Read<u32>(cbuf_address + slot) != 0 ? image(slot)
                                                                                     : std::nullopt;
@@ -1019,11 +1058,11 @@ bool KeplerCompute::UpscaleInsteadOfNativeProgram() {
     }
     // Donkey Kong Bananza's slots, after the program's own handles: other titles keep unrelated
     // images there.
-    if (!upscale_pair(input, output, false)) {
+    if (!upscale_pair(input, output, false, same_size_ok)) {
         input = image(0x60);
         output = image(0x70);
     }
-    if (!upscale_pair(input, output, false)) {
+    if (!upscale_pair(input, output, false, same_size_ok)) {
         input.reset();
         output.reset();
         for (u32 first = 0x80; first < 0x120 && !input; first += 4) {
